CELL_V1 — THE COMPLETE BUILD

---

1. THE CELL

Three differential pairs. One per axis. A, B, C.

Each pair IS a phase winding. Three pairs = three phases = the motor.

The toroid reads the three leans. It decides flip or hold. Its state determines which pairs fire next. The pairs switch. The motor turns. The lattice remembers.

Two hysteresis layers. Both write. Both remember. Both evolve through use.

No chips. No comparators. No op-amps. No diodes. No resistors in the signal path.

Everything gated. Heat is working temperature. Every flip is new view old action.

---

2. THE DIFFERENTIAL PAIRS — THE WINDINGS

One pair per axis. Three pairs per cell. Each pair is a phase winding.

```
                  V_TOP
                    │
           ┌────────┴────────┐
           │                 │
       [gated load]      [gated load]
           │                 │
          D_A               D_B
           │                 │
        ┌──┴──┐           ┌──┴──┐
  S+ ───┤ G   │           │   G ├─── S−
        │ Q1  │           │  Q2 │
        │  D  │           │  D  │
        └──┬──┘           └──┬──┘
           │                 │
           └────────┬────────┘
                    │
              [gated tail]
                    │
                  V_BUS
```

Q1, Q2: ALD1106 matched pair.

Loads: gated current sources (MOSFET).
Tail: gated current source (MOSFET).

No resistors. No diodes.

The three pairs are A, B, C. They are the motor's three phases. There is no separate motor downstream. The cell's own pairs are the phases.

The switching of these pairs IS the H-bridge function. The pairs commutate in sequence. PUSH on A, PULL on B, HOLD on C, then rotate. Six steps. The toroid's state provides the order.

---

3. THE GEOMETRY

Flat-top hexagon. Six edges. Three mirror pairs.

Clockwise from the top:

Position Edge
Top A+
Upper-right B+
Lower-right C+
Bottom A−
Lower-left B−
Upper-left C−

Mirror pairs (directly opposite through the center):

· A+ (top) ↔ A− (bottom)
· B+ (upper-right) ↔ B− (lower-left)
· C+ (lower-right) ↔ C− (upper-left)

CENTER in the middle.

V_TOP above. V_BUS below.

Edge centers, not corners.

