8. THE WINDINGS

The windings are the differential pairs. Three pairs, three phases.

· Pair A = phase A winding
· Pair B = phase B winding
· Pair C = phase C winding

The sense winding (10 turns, 36 AWG) on the toroid reads the combined flux from the three pairs.

The toroid's drive winding (50 turns, 30 AWG) carries the sense current. It does not drive the pairs.

The pairs drive the motor. The toroid reads them.

