11. MEMORY IS THE REFERENCE

No separate reference circuit.

The square figure-8 toroid's flipped state is the reference.

The lattice's accumulated path is the reference depth.

Every write is a reference update. Every reference update is a memory write.

The baseline zero is the memory. Two cells with different histories have different references. You cannot copy the reference.

---

12. THE LATTICE WRITES ITS OWN PATH

Every write deepens the path. The next event follows the same route more easily. The route evolves through use.

· First write: shallow trace.
· Repeated writes: path deepens.
· Over time: the path is preferred.

Not memory as a snapshot. Memory as a groove that wears in.

Evolution through use. The substrate changes because of its own history.

The lattice is:

· Muscle memory — the accumulated path
· Distributed intelligence — coupling across cells
· Body state — the combined pattern
· Strain signal — saturation, sag, thermal load

Silent during normal operation. Tops off the bus. Balances. Only danger thresholds or reflex inputs trip a binary signal.

---

13. REINJECTION — EVERYTHING GATED

No diodes.

When a pair's winding collapses, the same MOSFETs that drove it become the steering path. They turn on and route current to V_BUS. Same MOSFETs. Different phase.

```
    Every collapse path
         │
         ▼
    Gate (pair MOSFETs)
         │
         ▼
    C_BUS → V_BUS
```

Six gates per cell. One per edge. Every waste path has a gate to the bus.

Gated: winding collapse, switching transients, stray capacitance, back-EMF, vortex relaxation.
Not gated: I²R in copper, gate quiescent current, ferrite losses.

Heat is working temperature. Ferrite has an operating window. The heat that isn't gated keeps the cell in it.

---

14. THE POWER RAILS

No resistors. Gated references.

V_TOP — quiet analog headroom.

CENTER — the reference. Read from the toroid's flipped state. Not a divider. Not a bandgap.

V_BUS — living rail. Catches every collapse.

```
    BATTERY (3.7V LiPo)
        │
        ▼
    REGULATOR (LDO, 1.8V) → V_TOP
        │
        ├────── toroid state read → CENTER
        │
        ▼
    ASK SWITCH (MOSFET) → V_BUS
        │
        ▼
    C_BUS (1µF)
```

